Package: gc2607-isp
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: mesa-vulkan-drivers, v4l2loopback-dkms, gc2607-driver-dkms, gc2607-ipu-bridge-dkms
Description: software ISP for the GalaxyCore GC2607 colour camera (on-demand webcam)
 gc2607-video captures raw Bayer frames from the GalaxyCore GC2607 (Huawei
 MateBook X Pro 2024, Intel IPU6) via libcamera, runs a full ISP (black level,
 lens-shading, AWB, debayer, colour-correction, sRGB) on the CPU or the GPU, and
 publishes the result to a v4l2loopback node as an on-demand virtual webcam: the
 sensor and ISP run only while an application is capturing.
 .
 This package ships a prebuilt binary that links against libcamera 0.7, so it
 targets Ubuntu 26.04. The GC2607 sensor driver and the patched ipu-bridge
 (separate packages) and a v4l2loopback module are required for a working camera.
